   <span class="eyebrow">&#128274; Privacy &amp; trust</span>
   <h1>Your learning belongs to you.</h1>
   <p>This policy explains, in plain language, what K Education collects, why we need it, who helps us provide the service, and the choices available to students and families.</p>
   <div class="meta"><span>Effective: 14 August 2026</span><span>Applies to the K Education app and website</span><span>Children and families included</span></div>
  </div>

  <div class="layout">
   <aside class="toc" aria-label="Policy contents"><strong>On this page</strong><nav>
    <a href="#scope">1. Scope</a><a href="#collection">2. Data we collect</a><a href="#use">3. How we use data</a><a href="#sharing">4. Service providers</a><a href="#children">5. Children &amp; families</a><a href="#security">6. Security</a><a href="#retention">7. Retention</a><a href="#choices">8. Your choices</a><a href="#deletion">9. Account deletion</a><a href="#changes">10. Changes</a><a href="#contact">11. Contact us</a>
   </nav></aside>

   <div class="content">
    <div class="summary" aria-label="Privacy highlights">
     <article><span>&#128683;</span><strong>No targeted advertising</strong><small>We do not sell personal information or use student data for targeted ads.</small></article>
     <article><span>&#128272;</span><strong>Encrypted in transit</strong><small>The production service uses HTTPS to protect information while it travels.</small></article>
     <article><span>&#9003;</span><strong>Deletion available</strong><small>Users can permanently delete their account and associated active-service data.</small></article>
    </div>

    <article class="policy">
     <section id="scope"><h2>1. Who we are and what this policy covers</h2><p>K Education is an educational service for Sri Lankan students, with learning content, quizzes, progress tools, parent access and an AI-assisted tutor. This Privacy Policy applies when you use the K Education Android application, progressive web application, website and related parent services.</p><p>“K Education”, “we”, “us” and “our” refer to the K Education developer shown on the Google Play listing.</p></section>

     <section id="collection"><h2>2. Information we collect</h2><p>We collect only information used to provide, secure and improve the learning service.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Examples</th><th>Why it is needed</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td>Account and personal information</td><td>Name, phone number, generated username/user ID, school, district, grade, learning medium and preferred language. Parent accounts also provide a name and email address. A referral code may be provided voluntarily.</td><td>Create and verify accounts, select suitable learning content, connect parent access and provide support.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Learning and app activity</td><td>Lessons opened or completed, quiz answers and scores, progress, points, achievements, searches and feature actions.</td><td>Run learning features, save progress, personalize the experience and show progress to the student and an authorized linked parent.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>AI Tutor content</td><td>Questions, prompts, selected subject or lesson context, language and AI-generated responses.</td><td>Answer learning questions, maintain chat history and provide grade-appropriate assistance.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Profile photo</td><td>An optional image selected by the user.</td><td>Personalize the account profile.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Subscription and purchase records</td><td>Plan, amount, payment method, transaction or receipt reference, status and subscription dates.</td><td>Review a voluntary Premium purchase, prevent duplicate or fraudulent claims and activate access. We do not collect card numbers or online-banking passwords.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Technical information</td><td>IP address, browser or app user-agent, session cookies and security/request information.</td><td>Deliver the service, maintain sessions, measure downloads, prevent abuse and diagnose technical problems.</td></tr>
     </tbody></table></div><p>We do not request precise GPS location, contacts, calendar, microphone recordings, health information or advertising identifiers. The district supplied during registration and location that may be inferred from an IP address are considered approximate location.</p></section>

     <section id="use"><h2>3. How we use information</h2><ul><li>Provide accounts, authentication, lessons, quizzes, subscriptions, AI Tutor and parent-access functionality.</li><li>Choose content that matches a student’s registered grade, medium and language.</li><li>Save and display progress, results, learning streaks, points and achievements.</li><li>Send a one-time verification code and protect accounts against misuse.</li><li>Review payment references submitted for Premium activation.</li><li>Maintain security, troubleshoot errors, understand feature use and comply with applicable obligations.</li></ul><div class="notice"><strong>We do not sell personal information.</strong> We do not use children’s personal information, AI Tutor messages or learning history for behavioral advertising.</div></section>

     <section id="sharing"><h2>4. When information is sent to service providers</h2><p>We use a limited number of providers to deliver specific functions. Information is sent only when needed for that function:</p><ul><li><strong>Text.lk:</strong> receives a phone number and verification-message details to deliver account OTP messages.</li><li><strong>Google Gemini and/or OpenAI:</strong> receives an AI Tutor prompt, recent relevant conversation, selected lesson context, grade and language so it can generate a response. Users should not enter secrets or unnecessary personal information in AI Tutor questions.</li><li><strong>Hosting and infrastructure providers:</strong> process information necessary to host the K Education website, database and application securely.</li></ul><p>These providers may process information in countries other than the user’s country. Their handling is also governed by their applicable terms and privacy commitments. We may disclose information where legally required, to protect users and the service, or as part of a business transfer with appropriate safeguards. We do not share information with advertising networks.</p></section>

     <section id="children"><h2>5. Children and families</h2><p>K Education is designed to support school-age learners and is committed to following the Google Play Families Policy. We limit collection to information used for education, account security and service operation; do not show targeted advertising; and provide parent-linking tools without making a student’s profile public.</p><p>A parent or guardian should help a child understand this policy and supervise account creation where appropriate. A parent or guardian who believes a child submitted information improperly may contact us to request review or deletion.</p></section>

     <section id="security"><h2>6. How we protect information</h2><p>We use HTTPS encryption in transit, password hashing, access controls, authenticated sessions, CSRF protection, input validation, restricted administrative access and other reasonable technical and organizational safeguards. No online system can guarantee absolute security, so users should keep passwords and OTP codes private and contact us if they suspect unauthorized access.</p></section>

     <section id="retention"><h2>7. How long we keep information</h2><p>Account, profile, learning, chat and subscription information is generally retained while the account remains active so that the service can preserve learning progress and account access. OTP codes expire within minutes. Operational and security records are retained only as reasonably necessary for their stated purposes.</p><p>After account deletion, associated data is removed from the active service. Limited copies may remain in encrypted backups or security logs for up to 90 days before scheduled removal, unless a longer period is required for fraud prevention, dispute resolution, security or law.</p></section>

     <section id="choices"><h2>8. Your privacy choices</h2><ul><li>Profile photos, AI Tutor use, referral codes and Premium purchases are optional.</li><li>Users can review and update supported profile details from their account.</li><li>Users can avoid submitting personal information inside AI Tutor questions.</li><li>A student controls parent access through the account-linking process.</li><li>Users or guardians may contact us with a privacy question or correction request.</li></ul></section>

     <section id="deletion"><h2>9. Account and data deletion</h2><p>A signed-in student can permanently delete the account and associated active-service data, including profile information, profile photo, learning progress, quiz records, AI Tutor conversations, activity history, parent links and subscription records.</p><p><a href="delete-account.php">Open the K Education account-deletion page</a> for instructions and the deletion pathway. If you cannot sign in, contact us using the privacy address below.</p></section>

     <section id="changes"><h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2><p>We may update this policy when the app, providers or legal requirements change. We will publish the revised policy here and update the effective date. Material changes may also be communicated through the app or another appropriate notice.</p></section>

     <section id="contact"><h2>11. Contact us</h2><div class="contact"><strong>K Education Privacy</strong><p>For privacy questions, parent or guardian requests, corrections, or help with deletion, email <a href="mailto:privacy@keducation.site">privacy@keducation.site</a>.</p><p>Please do not email passwords, OTP codes or full banking details.</p></div></section>
    </article>
